   "agent": "auto",
   "tier": "mid",
   "prompt": "Bug reported from the atlas-seafloor project: swarm go --scope ran ticket T-0060 on branch swarm/boi; the wave summary said status committed and a later 'swarm integrate RUN --queue' answered 'Run already integrated' for run 1792767715925-95e62ad1, but the target file tests/browser/test_standalone_offline.py (a Python file) has zero diff against the previous commit and the journal has no integrate commit for that run. The worker's result (swarm inspect RUN --results) correctly reports the intended file_changed with a sane note, so the worker did its job; the integrate step never wrote or committed the output, yet reported success. The owner had to hand-apply the one-line change. Investigate tools/swarm.mjs (the integrate path, around the 'Run already integrated' checks near line 1545, the integrationStatus recording, and the part that decides a job's outputs are 'byte for byte what the tree already has: nothing to write') and tools/scope-commands.mjs (the wave integrate and sync that print 'committed'). Find every way integrate can mark a job or run integrated while the tree and the branch do not contain the job's output bytes (for example: the base-hash comparison treating the output as already present because the worker workspace was seeded from a newer copy, an output compared against the wrong root or the wrong worktree, a .py or other non-JS path filtered by an ignore or protected rule, an integrate done in a different worktree than the branch's, the 'nothing to write' shortcut firing when the file differs only by trailing newline or file mode). Add a regression test in tests/integrate-silent-noop.test.mjs that reproduces at least the most plausible cause with a real temp git repo and a fake finished run (follow the fixtures in tests/integrate-safety.test.mjs and tests/integrate-hashes.test.mjs), then fix it. Independently of the root cause, add a post-write verification: after integrate reports integrated, re-read every output from the tree and compare its bytes with the job's output (or with HEAD when the files were committed); on a mismatch do NOT record the run or job as integrated, report 'integrate-no-op: PATH differs from the job output' as an error, and leave the run re-integratable. The scope sync and the wave summary must only say committed when that verification passed. Keep tests/integrate-*.test.mjs, tests/scope-sync*.test.mjs and tests/lesson-39-integrate.test.mjs passing.",
